value &= ~GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_RA;
if (dev->flags & IFF_PROMISC) {
    value = GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_PR | GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_RA;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the Receive All (RA) bit is not cleared when promiscuous mode is turned off. The first statement attempts to clear the RA bit, but it is immediately overwritten by the second statement when promiscuous mode is enabled, leading to the device continuing to receive all packets even when it should not.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
value &= ~GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_RA;
if (!(dev->flags & IFF_PROMISC)) {
    value &= ~GMAC_PACKET_FILTER_RA;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the RA bit is explicitly cleared when promiscuous mode is turned off. By adding a condition to check if promiscuous mode is not enabled, the RA bit will be cleared appropriately, preventing the device from receiving all packets when it should only receive those intended for it.

